%%{init: {'theme':'default'}}%%
%% End-to-end postal campaign + QR reconciliation flow (Epic #274).
%% Companion to `docs/23-postal-campaigns.md`.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Op as Operator (org_admin)
    participant Web as Next.js (web)
    participant API as Fastify (api)
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant Outbox as Outbox relay
    participant Worker as BullMQ worker
    participant S3 as Object storage
    actor Donor

    rect rgb(245, 248, 250)
      Note over Op,Web: 1. Curate the recipient list
      Op->>Web: Add constituents via dialog
      Web->>API: POST /campaigns/:id/constituents
      API->>DB: INSERT campaign_constituents (idempotent)
    end

    rect rgb(245, 248, 250)
      Note over Op,Web: 2. Validate the layout
      Op->>Web: Click "Aperçu PDF"
      Web->>API: POST /campaigns/:id/postal-preview
      API-->>Web: PDF (Jean Dupont fixture)
      Web->>Donor: open in new tab
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 230)
      Note over Op,Worker: 3. Async ZIP generation
      Op->>Web: Click "Generate ZIP"
      Web->>API: POST /campaigns/:id/postal-exports
      API->>DB: INSERT pending row + outbox event
      API-->>Web: 202 + exportId
      Outbox->>Worker: Enqueue job
      Worker->>DB: UPDATE status=processing
      loop Per recipient
        Worker->>DB: INSERT campaign_qr_codes
        Worker->>S3: Stream PDF into archive
        Worker->>DB: progress_count++ (live)
      end
      Worker->>S3: Finalise multipart upload
      Worker->>DB: UPDATE status=completed
      Web-->>Op: Download link
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 244)
      Note over Op,Donor: 4. Print → distribute
      Op->>Op: Send ZIP to print shop
      Op->>Donor: Postal letter delivered
    end

    rect rgb(232, 240, 254)
      Note over Donor,API: 5. Scan + donate
      Donor->>Web: Scan QR → /p/:id?qr=<token>
      Web->>API: GET /v1/public/qr/<token>
      API->>DB: UPDATE scanned_at (first scan only)
      API-->>Web: { campaignId, constituentId? }
      Donor->>Web: Submit donation form
      Web->>API: POST /v1/public/.../donate { qrCode }
      API->>API: Resolve qrCode → Stripe metadata<br/>(qr_code_id, qr_code_constituent_id)
    end

    rect rgb(252, 232, 232)
      Note over API,DB: 6. Webhook reconciliation
      API->>API: Stripe webhook checkout.completed
      API->>DB: INSERT donations<br/>(campaign_id, constituent_id, qr_code_id)
      API->>DB: Update QR attribution stats
    end
